{"body":"Requests such as “show deltas” calculated change facts locally but omitted them from the messages sent to the live provider. The guarded prompt now includes the existing delta summary inside its untrusted-data block, sanitizes source instructions and boundary markers, and caps that section at 4,000 characters with an explicit truncation marker.\n\nCloses #1064\n\n## Tasks\n- [x] Serialize loaded change facts into guarded provider messages.\n- [x] Exercise ChatSession through the actual LangChainProviderClient and ChatOpenAI construction, intercepting only ChatOpenAI.invoke.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] `python -m pytest tests/test_chat_provider_clients.py -q` — 27 passed; `test_delta_facts_reach_langchain_invoke` finds DeltaOnlyBank and delta_notional=876543.21 inside the untrusted block of actual messages.\n- [x] Ordinary top-exposure queries and conversation history remain supported without network calls.\n- [x] Hostile instruction text, literal boundary tokens, empty deltas, and oversized source names are covered at the transport boundary.\n- [x] Deliberate-break gate: removing the TOP_DELTAS prompt field made all 3 named transport regression cases fail; restoring it passed the complete focused suite.\n\n## Validation\n- `python -m pytest tests/test_chat_provider_clients.py tests/test_chat_session.py tests/test_chat_context.py -q` — 117 passed.\n- Focused Ruff, Black, production-module mypy, and `git diff --check` passed.\n- Local execution reused existing LangChain dependencies alongside the parser test environment; no live provider request was made.\n- Evidence: opener run `20260920T010132Z`, `chat-acceptance.txt`, `chat-deliberate-break.txt`, `chat-restored-suite.txt`.\n\n<!-- deliberate-break: test=tests/test_chat_provider_clients.py::test_delta_facts_reach_langchain_invoke test-file=tests/test_chat_provider_clients.py break-file=src/counter_risk/chat/session.py -->\n\n<!-- pr-preamble:start -->\n<!-- meta:issue:1064 -->\n> **Source:** Issue #1064\n\nCloses #1064\n\n<!-- pr-preamble:end -->\n\n<!-- auto-status-summary:start -->\n## Automated Status Summary\n#### Scope\n`src/counter_risk/chat/session.py:292` is current evidence at current main 7c01963cb4173128c806347e622ed43a08fdcf4a. Current break at the transport boundary: asking show deltas computes DeltaOnlyBank delta_notional=876543.21 locally, but that name and value never reach LangChain invoke. `build_guarded_prompt` includes summary/warnings/top exposures only (`src/counter_risk/chat/session.py:404`), and `src/counter_risk/chat/providers/base.py:133` invokes the provider with messages while ignoring context_answer. Offline providers and test doubles consume context_answer, masking the missing facts. No live model response or external API call was used to establish this payload omission.\n\n<!-- Updated WORKFLOW_OUTPUTS.md context:start -->\n## Context for Agent\n\n### Related Issues/PRs\n- [#108](https://github.com/stranske/Counter_Risk/issues/108)\n- [#25](https://github.com/stranske/Counter_Risk/issues/25)\n- [#1036](https://github.com/stranske/Counter_Risk/issues/1036)\n<!-- Updated WORKFLOW_OUTPUTS.md context:end -->\n\n#### Tasks\n- [x] In `src/counter_risk/chat/session.py`, serialize the requested delta facts into guarded message content before provider invocation, using existing sanitization and data boundaries.\n- [x] In `tests/test_chat_provider_clients.py`, add `test_delta_facts_reach_langchain_invoke`. Exercise ChatSession through the actual LangChainProviderClient with only the final client.invoke transport intercepted; assert the name and value are in messages and malicious source strings remain untrusted.\n\n#### Acceptance criteria\n- [x] `python -m pytest tests/test_chat_provider_clients.py -q` passes and collects `test_delta_facts_reach_langchain_invoke`. The named transport test finds DeltaOnlyBank and 876543.21 in the actual messages for show deltas; ordinary top-exposure queries remain supported without network access.\n- [x] Deliberate-break gate: temporarily restore the faulty behavior in `src/counter_risk/chat/session.py`; `tests/test_chat_provider_clients.py::test_delta_facts_reach_langchain_invoke` must fail; revert the deliberate break and rerun the named test to pass. Capture both outcomes in the implementation PR.\n- [x] The test exercises the actual production boundary and retains a valid-input control.\n\n<!-- auto-status-summary:end -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n- **Security & Reliability**\n  - Improved prompt handling by masking sensitive boundary markers before displaying delta information.\n  - Limited serialized delta content to 4,000 characters to keep prompts bounded.\n  - Preserved accurate handling of message history and empty delta results.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","closingIssuesReferences":[{"id":"I_kwDORPCqTs8AAAABRJ7sGA","number":1064,"repository":{"id":"R_kgDORPCqTg","name":"Counter_Risk","owner":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDQ2MzIy","login":"stranske"}},"url":"https://github.com/stranske/Counter_Risk/issues/1064"}],"labels":[{"id":"LA_kwDORPCqTs8AAAACX8Y9vQ","name":"agent:codex","description":"Assign to Codex agent","color":"0e8a16"},{"id":"LA_kwDORPCqTs8AAAACX8Y-KA","name":"agents:keepalive","description":"Enable keepalive monitoring on PR","color":"1d76db"},{"id":"LA_kwDORPCqTs8AAAACX8Y-aw","name":"autofix","description":"Let bots format/lint automatically","color":"0366d6"},{"id":"LA_kwDORPCqTs8AAAACX8esvQ","name":"verify:compare","description":"Runs verifier comparison mode after merge","color":"1D76DB"},{"id":"LA_kwDORPCqTs8AAAACpd5UZQ","name":"codex","description":"","color":"ededed"}],"mergeCommit":{"oid":"9d3187af1e7dc9ad65e1b879c58e103872f7251f"},"mergedAt":"2026-09-20T01:44:00Z","statusCheckRollup":[{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-20T01:25:34Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/stranske/Counter_Risk/